philippine right now a utv crash on  christmas eve leaves one man in custody  26 year old yasmani flamen is facing  reckless driving charges but tonight his  sister the victim in this incident says  her brother doesn't deserve the blame  madison kimbrough is at umc with her  story  isabella was in the passenger seat when  the wreck occurred on friday and now  she's here at umc where she had to have  her right arm amputated after the utv  crashed rolled onto its side and flipped  upwards it being less than two days  since the crash isabella wants people to  know that the crash was an accident and  that her brother 26 year old yasmani  flemen is not to blame flemen is the one  who lost control of the vehicle that  christmas eve night isabella says she  and the rest of the family are upset  with how nlvpd handled the situation and  don't want her brother labeled as a  criminal after being arrested and  charged for reckless driving the first  voice i heard was my brother's he said  sister are you okay it was unjustified  there was no reason for him to go to  jail we had just pulled into the parking  lot he was going at 26. he had he wasn't  drinking that night he wasn't he wasn't  on anything he was completely sober  other than isabella and her brother two  other people were in the u-t-v one being  isabella's boyfriend who suffered  non-life-threatening injuries we plan on  talking to him later tonight reporting  from umc madison kimbrough live local  now
 

